  "subtitle": "A coin-op reflex machine whose interface is a life-size picture you physically strike at lit target points on a martial-arts combatant.",
  "why_scout_cares": "The earliest arcade reflex-striking device — a two-player coin-op machine where the input is a full-body physical strike on a life-size picture, at lights sunk into 10 attack/defense points. Pure 7400-series TTL logic, no CPU. Distinct from every punch-pad/foot-controller exhibit in the museum.",
  "search_terms": ["Brunswick Karate 1974 arcade reflex machine", "US3933354 reflex testing amusement device", "Brunswick coin-op karate picture lights microswitch"],
